d 2002, primarily releases limited-edition live recordings offered as free downloads (Live at The Belmont 2010, Live at Short's 2006). Dashboard Confessional is an American emo/alternative act, released a live album MTV Unplugged 2.0 in 2002 that went platinum and charted #111 on Billboard 200, and released radio singles in 2006 such as \"Rooftops and Invitations\" and \"Don't Wait\". Provide answer summarizing differences.\n\nWe need citations: For Escanaba formation: sentence 0 title Escanaba Firing Line. For live albums: Live at the Belmont sentence 1; Live at Short's sentence 1. For Dashboard: MTV Unplugged 2.0 sentence 0 (live album), sentence 3 (platinum), sentence 5 (peaked #111). For singles: \"Rooftops and Invitations\" sentence 2 (release date), \"Don't Wait\" sentence 3 (release date). Could also include sentence 0 for \"Don't Wait\" but not needed.\n\nAnswer must be concise but include key comparison. Provide JSON with answer and citations list.\n\nMake answer: \"Escanaba Firing Line is a Michigan rock band formed in 2002 that issues only limited‑edition live recordings such as Live at the Belmont (2010) and Live at Short’s (2006), both released as free downloads, whereas Dashboard Confessional is an American emo/alternative act whose 2002 live album MTV Unplugged 2.0 was certified platinum and reached #111 on the Billboard 200, and who released radio singles in 2006 like “Rooftops and Invitations” and “Don’t Wait”.\" Provide citations accordingly.\n\nCitations list: each as [title, sentence_index].\n\nList: [\"Escanaba Firing Line\",0], [\"Live at the Belmont\",1], [\"Live at Short's 2005\",1], [\"MTV Unplugged 2.0\",0], [\"MTV Unplugged 2.0\",3], [\"MTV Unplugged 2.0\",5], [\"Rooftops and Invitations\",2], [\"Don't Wait (Dashboard Confessional song)\",3].\n\nReturn JSON."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1370,"completion_tokens":937,"total_tokens":2307,"audio_prompt_tokens":0},"created":1791970207,"object":"chat.completion","prompt_fi